# dist/ is the deploy-time staging tree from build/make-dist.js — normally
# shipped on its own via `wrangler pages deploy dist`, never as part of a raw
# `wrangler pages deploy .`. Without this line, a raw deploy from the repo
# root would also upload whatever dist/ happens to be sitting on disk
# (13k+ files) on top of the ~13k real repo files, blowing past Cloudflare
# Pages' 20,000-file limit — exactly when "the emergency fallback" is needed.
